message.content:
Below is a minimal example of an “interactive card” that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Container that gives perspective to the card */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
    perspective: 800px;          /* Creates a 3D space */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* Needed for 3D children */
    position: relative;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;      /* Hide backside when rotated */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
    border-radius: 12px;
}

/* Back side – rotated 180° so it’s hidden initially */
.card .back {
    background: #f8f8f8;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="front">Front Side</div>
        <div class="back">Back Side</div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective: 800px`). |
| `.card` | Holds both sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Both occupy the same space; `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side facing away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° on the Y‑axis so it starts hidden. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the entire card 180°, revealing the back side. |

You can replace the text inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any other content you like. Adjust the `perspective`, `transition`, and `border-radius` values to fit your design.
